editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:33:[[TIER-B: "there" — the packet names this as the word at which the twelfth arrives ("the acquisition at 'there'") and gives neither its sentence nor its speaker; staged as the next thing said over the Stair's ninth sheet, at the moment when Cleon's finger comes to rest above the end of the fifth row. The paragraphs after this line are written so that Cleon or Karis could own the word. If the word falls inside Cleon's speech above, strike this marker and let Karis's "The strata lean too." follow the acquisition; coordinator to supply protected text]]
