editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:122:4. **The Deepstacks decipherment** (≈8,000). The chamber days 285–292 are put on the page, including the undramatized 288th–289th. Cleon's method (bones before words), the board's numerals, Karis's letters coming one at a time from the three floors, and the lamp's discipline. Karis refuses to guess. **The leaf must not become readable on the page before the seventh day** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:174:| 6 | Before the Paths | 34–40 | 34,000 | S13, S14, S15, S16 | The twelfth and the warning; dividers and the light's wrong count; the leaf read once; pole two at the fire. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:194:| **Karis** | ≈7,500 (3) | M1: a cold night [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] with the kit's index (her want; the cord reads wrong only for him, and she refuses a theory). M5: decipherment (board numerals; the first letters). M8: the night after the lamps finding (the refusal held in her own head). | The sheets; strata; the index (as unreadable until the 298th); the leaf (after the 293rd); the lamps finding. | The Rune finding (nobody knows it). The integration of Rune before Cael tells Lira. **Drawing the line**: her interior names that the sentence exists and refuses it. The deep-layer date as Cael's Kindling. The leaf's content before it is read aloud. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:196:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:233:| 293 | The leaf read aloud (morning); the yard fire (evening) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:333:- **The leaf is read aloud once**, by Karis, in the chamber, on the 293rd morning (M6). It is not quoted again by anyone who heard it. Cael gives Lira the page to read; nobody says it back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:338:- **Two pages, no line.** The leaf and the lamps finding are never joined: not in dialogue, not in any interior (including cutaways), not in the narration. Vastin's sentence stops twice (in the chamber; on the shale). The words *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* are never used for Arbiters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:343:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:345:Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:347:### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:349:1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:350:2. **The chronicle (S15):** "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" [a thumb's width of hole]. Karis: "Marked." Cleon: "Marked."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:351:3. **Karis's copy and finding (S15):** "and the" [gap drawn] "set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it." / *Older. Made. Us.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:358:10. **Cleon's warning (S13):** "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that," he said, "for your sake, not mine. But I'll tell you one thing for free, since you can apparently take my whole trade by watching me work it for a minute." … "Everything I read is *made*. Stone, ink, seal — somebody built it, so I can see how. If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — " He stopped. "Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it." Chapter-close sentence: "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:361:13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:364:15. **Hesk's dividers note (S14):** "A rule says a line is true. A divider says how far, and carries it. You've the first. Here's the second, and mind the points; they'll go through a thumb as easy as a sheet. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. — H."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:366:17. **Pole two (S16):** Lira: "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Cael: "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." / Lira: "Yeah." … "Now what." / Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is. Karis has a bearing and the marks, and the records to read them against. There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." … "I want to stand in the middle of it." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:367:18. **Vastin at the fire (S16):** "I believed it was imperfect." … "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*." … "At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." / Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I did." / "His?" / "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." / "Yes," Lira said. "You would have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:378:### Tier B — earlier books' wording quoted here (binding from source)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:389:### Tier C — source-fixed lines and closers (keep verbatim)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:403:- **S13:** "An instruction *leans*." … "This is a stair." / "The strata lean too." / "Twelfth. His. Lean." / "You did what." / "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's — " / "No," … "No. I'll not say that one. Not down here. Not to you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:404:- **S14 log lines:** "Hesk sent dividers. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. I'll enter that as a rule and see what it's worth." / "The promise stands. Not the steps. Not the square." Also: "Out here you count who's owed a seat," … "It's a different ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:426:| The Architect's will is active and hunting Cael | 11 | Three deniable plant families only: (1) the running sub-layer sequence (S3/S5); (2) "is in it —", marked (S15); (3) the instruments and the station clustering on Cael, trending up (S1/S5/S14/S22, plus the Span row). Attributed in-world to his unreadability. "Made things do not know." Nothing says or implies agency. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:447:- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:452:- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:473:- **Karis cannot read the index as a grade** until the 298th. The leaf is not readable on the page before the seventh day of Cleon's week.
