editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:609:[[TIER-B: Cleon's warning (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 10): "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that," he said, "for your sake, not mine. But I'll tell you one thing for free, since you can apparently take my whole trade by watching me work it for a minute." … "Everything I read is *made*. Stone, ink, seal — somebody built it, so I can see how. If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — " He stopped. "Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it." — the plan gives the unit with an elision between its halves; staged as Cleon's, said at the third table after he has set the cup of water down, to the board and not to Cael's face; coordinator to supply protected text]]
