editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2219:[[TIER-B: Vastin: "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." — the plan gives this answer with an elision (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 18); staged as Vastin's reply to Lira's "His?", said across the fire from the mounting block; coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2257:[[TIER-B: Pole two, Cael's sentence (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 17): "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." — the plan gives this speech in three pieces with elisions; staged as Cael's, said aloud on his feet at the fire-basket in the inn's yard, to all of them and to nobody in particular, with Hesk's book left in his coat; he does not write it down afterward; coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2269:[[TIER-B: Pole two, Lira (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 17): "Yeah." … "Now what." — the plan gives her two lines with an elision between them; staged as Lira's, from her bucket, the first thing said by anybody after Cael's sentence; coordinator to supply protected text]]
