editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3055:- **Two pages, no line.** The leaf and the lamps finding are never joined: not in dialogue, not in any interior (including cutaways), not in the narration. Vastin's sentence stops twice (in the chamber; on the shale). The words *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* are never used for Arbiters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3060:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3062:Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3064:### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3066:1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3067:2. **The chronicle (S15):** "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" [a thumb's width of hole]. Karis: "Marked." Cleon: "Marked."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3068:3. **Karis's copy and finding (S15):** "and the" [gap drawn] "set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it." / *Older. Made. Us.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3075:10. **Cleon's warning (S13):** "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that," he said, "for your sake, not mine. But I'll tell you one thing for free, since you can apparently take my whole trade by watching me work it for a minute." … "Everything I read is *made*. Stone, ink, seal — somebody built it, so I can see how. If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — " He stopped. "Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it." Chapter-close sentence: "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3078:13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3081:15. **Hesk's dividers note (S14):** "A rule says a line is true. A divider says how far, and carries it. You've the first. Here's the second, and mind the points; they'll go through a thumb as easy as a sheet. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. — H."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3083:17. **Pole two (S16):** Lira: "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Cael: "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." / Lira: "Yeah." … "Now what." / Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is. Karis has a bearing and the marks, and the records to read them against. There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." … "I want to stand in the middle of it." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3084:18. **Vastin at the fire (S16):** "I believed it was imperfect." … "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*." … "At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." / Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I did." / "His?" / "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." / "Yes," Lira said. "You would have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3095:### Tier B — earlier books' wording quoted here (binding from source)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3106:### Tier C — source-fixed lines and closers (keep verbatim)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3120:- **S13:** "An instruction *leans*." … "This is a stair." / "The strata lean too." / "Twelfth. His. Lean." / "You did what." / "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's — " / "No," … "No. I'll not say that one. Not down here. Not to you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3121:- **S14 log lines:** "Hesk sent dividers. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. I'll enter that as a rule and see what it's worth." / "The promise stands. Not the steps. Not the square." Also: "Out here you count who's owed a seat," … "It's a different ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3143:| The Architect's will is active and hunting Cael | 11 | Three deniable plant families only: (1) the running sub-layer sequence (S3/S5); (2) "is in it —", marked (S15); (3) the instruments and the station clustering on Cael, trending up (S1/S5/S14/S22, plus the Span row). Attributed in-world to his unreadability. "Made things do not know." Nothing says or implies agency. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3156:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3164:- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3169:- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3190:- **Karis cannot read the index as a grade** until the 298th. The leaf is not readable on the page before the seventh day of Cleon's week.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3707:- **The decipherment (Karis alone).** Of the forty-one kinds of sign: **seven bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing**; the carried are what a word is spelled in. The plank's cutter counted each row in figures (a ring is five, a peck one) and then wrote the number out in words, in the old town's tongue or its near kin; she proved it against the old tally-books by pattern alone before looking. **Fourteen of twenty-three letters by the 290th; she reads numbers and number-words only**, has refused to guess one tempting six-sign word, has not untied the bundle, and has not shown Cleon Vastin's copied page (it is in her coat). **The leaf has not appeared.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4127:### The leaf — PROVISIONAL (the primary source, read Ch15; the reveal LOCKED as drafted)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4128:Under Treswick's registry, in the Deepstacks (the old quarry the walls were cut from; a single iron leaf on pins; Cleon's key), among a bundle Cleon pulled from the galleries thirty years ago: twelve horn-coloured point-written leaves older than the board. One passage, read aloud once by Karis: the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land; one who "made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling … and set the apparatus over all the land"; the name scraped to the fibre (four or five letters; the first stroke); "that the un-bound should not come again"; ~four hundred years by the leaf's head. **The Architect** is the record's TITLE for the maker (Karis: "a title, not a name; the name's gone"). A later chronicle leaf: "he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" then a thumb's width of nothing — MARKED, not read (Book 11's plant). The leaf's "list of parts" names the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in the same line ("A mark is a grade"). The leaf stays on Cleon's shelf; the crew carries copies with the gap drawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4189:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 23–26; §3 A (the tail), B 5; §5 (the Vastin and Oryn cutaways); §7.1 (Rune; the instruments); **§9 (all of it)**; §10 Tier A 1–3, 10, 13, 15, 17–18 and the S13–S16 Tier C lines; **§11**; §12 C10; §13.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4201:- **The reader (291st).** Cleon shows the Path from inside: "A record sits … An instruction *leans* … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." Then **the acquisition at "there"**. The fifth row leans, and so does the board, and Cael does not turn the twelfth on anything else. He tells Lira first on the stair ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then goes back down and tells Cleon at the bell, in the order he has it. "You did what." "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water, and **the warning, verbatim**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael carry the case up the stair together. **The notice on the stair, verbatim**, with *He looked away. Kept.* The eyes are paid on the last flight. **"Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4205:- **The leaf (293rd morning).** Describe the object before the reading: horn-coloured, point-written, the scraped name with its first upright stroke. Karis reads it **aloud once** (§9; §10 Tier A 1), then paraphrases it once: "the Architect" is a title, about four hundred years ago, and the purpose is the un-bound. "Older. Made. Us." Cael catalogues the room, not himself. **The chronicle** is marked: "Marked." / "Marked." Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers with **two pages** and the ruler rule. The copy, with the gap drawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4206:- **The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. Cael gives **Lira the page to read first**; nobody explains it to her. "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom prices it. Seln will keep the cache "a while longer". Karis says two pages, then sleeps on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, taken on his feet and not catalogued, verbatim. "I want to stand in the middle of it." Cleon leaves: "Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts."

